/-!
# Mathieu calculations for K.4

The native M23/M24 cocode part of K.4.1 is proved. The M22 restriction
calculations use the literal code hyperplane, the pair-line cocode quotient,
and their coordinate pairing; their ratio assemblies still take the exact
octad geometry explicitly. LinearSteps also supplies the ambient quadraticity
transfer needed in the M12 hyperplane argument.

The full K.4 Mathieu theorem remains open: the code part of K.4.1, K.4.2–3's
native sextet and octad geometry, the discharge of the M22 geometric premises,
the M12 application, and the triple-M22 non-FF conclusion are not asserted here.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith, combined manuscript (1 March 2004), K.4,
printed pp.457–460 (PDF pp.468–471).
-/
